<urn:atm:triage:finding/AM3-ACCEPT-LOOP-LEFTOVER>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AM3-ACCEPT-LOOP-LEFTOVER" ;
  triage:title "AM.3 left crates/atm-daemon/src/local_ipc_transport/accept_loop.rs undeleted, contradicting its own removal-ledger disposition" ;
  triage:description "AM.3's Deliverable 1 requires deleting 'superseded local UDS and loopback client/listener workers, manual accept/read/write loops, module exports, fixtures, docs, and dependencies named by the AM.1 ledger,' and AM1-RM-003's disposition asserts this family is 'Removed by AM.3.' The commit correctly deleted local_ipc_transport.rs, local_tcp_transport.rs, local_ipc_connection.rs, local_ipc_transport/request_worker.rs, local_ipc_transport/connection_workers.rs, and local_ipc_transport/shutdown.rs (7265 total lines), and removed the mod local_ipc_transport; declaration from lib.rs. However crates/atm-daemon/src/local_ipc_transport/accept_loop.rs (a manual UDS accept-loop worker defining take_accept_error/handle_shutdown_probe, importing interprocess::local_socket::Stream) was never deleted. It is now an orphan: its own super::{...} imports reference the parent module file that this same commit deleted, so the file cannot even resolve within a real module tree; it has zero mod declarations anywhere in the workspace and zero references. Independently confirmed by 5 sources: quality-mgr's own direct file-existence check, rust-best-practices-agent, ruthless-boundary-qa, arch-qa, and req-qa, all converging on this exact file during the same QA-1 round." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-am" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "deletion-completeness" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady false ;
  triage:closedAt "2026-08-10T19:35:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedBy "quality-mgr" ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-08-10T19:15:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AM-S3 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-08-10T18:40:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AM3-ACCEPT-LOOP-LEFTOVER/AM3-QA1-1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AM3-ACCEPT-LOOP-LEFTOVER/AM3-QA1-2> ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "1" .

